chem11AddSection("chem11-acids-bases-salts",{"id": "chem11-p243-bronsted-lowery", "title": "Figure 8.1 Autoionization of Water · 8.2 Bronsted–Lowery Definitions of Acids and Bases · Tidbit: Hydronium ion", "headingUrdu": "شکل 8.1 پانی کی خود آئنائزیشن · 8.2 تیزابوں اور اساسوں کی برونسٹڈ لوری تعریفیں · معلومات: ہائیڈرونیم آئن", "headingPashto": "شکل 8.1 د اوبو ځان آیونایزیشن · 8.2 د اسیدونو او القليو د برونسټډ-لوري تعریفونه · ځانګړې یادونه: هایدرونیم آیون", "sourceLanguage": "en", "source": {"pdfPage": 243, "printedPage": 238}, "auditStatus": "corrected; unresolved source", "flow": [{"type": "figure", "index": 0}, {"type": "paragraphs", "ids": ["chem11-p243-h82", "chem11-p243-a1", "chem11-p243-a2", "chem11-p243-t-h", "chem11-p243-t0", "chem11-p243-t1"]}, {"type": "figure", "index": 1}], "equations": [], "figures": [{"id": "chem11-p243-fig8-1", "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 215\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two water molecules reacting to form a hydronium ion and a hydroxide ion\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:540px;height:auto;background:#fff\"><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"90\" r=\"38\" fill=\"#c0305a\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"60\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"60\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111\">H₂O</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">+</text><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"90\" r=\"38\" fill=\"#c0305a\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"148\" cy=\"60\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"192\" cy=\"60\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111\">H₂O</text><path d=\"M230 85 h60 M230 98 h60\" stroke=\"#222\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"90\" r=\"38\" fill=\"#c0305a\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"56\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"382\" cy=\"56\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"126\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">+</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111\">H₃O</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">Hydronium Ion</text><text x=\"425\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">+</text><circle cx=\"480\" cy=\"90\" r=\"30\" fill=\"#c0305a\" stroke=\"#733\"/><circle cx=\"468\" cy=\"62\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#7ec8e8\" stroke=\"#733\"/><text x=\"480\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">−</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111\">OH⁻</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">Hydroxide Ion</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#a02040\">Figure 8.1 Autoionization (self) of Water</text></svg>", "caption": "Figure 8.1 Autoionization (self) of Water", "captionUrdu": "شکل 8.1 پانی کی خود آئنائزیشن (ازخود)", "captionPashto": "شکل 8.1 د اوبو ځان آیونایزیشن (ځان)", "labels": [{"en": "H₂O", "ur": "H₂O", "ps": "H₂O"}, {"en": "Hydronium ion", "ur": "ہائیڈرونیم آئن", "ps": "هایدرونیم آیون"}, {"en": "Hydroxide ion", "ur": "ہائیڈرو آکسائیڈ آئن", "ps": "هایدروکسایډ آیون"}], "sourceGap": {"note": "Space-filling molecular models redrawn as simple circles; colours and sizes approximate. The right edge of the figure is slightly clipped."}}, {"id": "chem11-p243-hydronium", "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 170\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A proton combining with a water molecule to form a hydronium ion\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:540px;height:auto;background:#fff\"><text x=\"40\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">H</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"Arial\">+</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">+</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">H</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">:Ö:</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">H</text><path d=\"M215 78 h80\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M285 70 l12 8 l-12 8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M320 30 h-10 v100 h10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">H:Ö:H</text><text x=\"352\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\">H</text><path d=\"M470 30 h10 v100 h-10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"490\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">+</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#111\">Hydronium Ion</text></svg>", "caption": "Formation of the hydronium ion: H⁺ + H₂O → [H₃O]⁺", "captionUrdu": "ہائیڈرونیم آئن کی تشکیل: H⁺ + H₂O → [H₃O]⁺", "captionPashto": "د هایدرونیم آیون جوړېدل: H⁺ + H₂O → [H₃O]⁺", "labels": [{"en": "Hydronium Ion", "ur": "ہائیڈرونیم آئن", "ps": "هایدرونیم آیون"}], "sourceGap": {"note": "Electron-dot drawing redrawn as a schematic; dot positions are not reproduced exactly. The right bracket is clipped."}}], "sourceNote": "Printed folio 238. The right edge is clipped by the page curl on the text lines and on the right end of Figure 8.1 and of the Tidbit diagram; clipped endings are marked [scan obscured] and not inferred. The pink italic definition is partly cut at the right. A CamScanner watermark crosses the page.", "sourceGap": {"note": "Right-edge clipping on text and figures; figures redrawn as schematics."}, "review": {"reviewedAtUtc": "2026-10-12T10:05:32.560315+00:00", "scope": "Chemistry p243", "unresolved": "Edge clipping; figures redrawn; translations need native review"}, "paras": [
chem11Pair("8.2 Bronsted – Lowery Definitions of Acids and Bases","8.2 تیزابوں اور اساسوں کی برونسٹڈ لوری تعریفیں","8.2 د اسیدونو او القليو د برونسټډ-لوري تعریفونه",{"id": "chem11-p243-h82", "kind": "heading"}),
chem11Pair("The limitations of the Arrhenius theory of acids and bases are overcom[scan obscured] by a more general concept, called the Bronsted-Lowery concept. The Bronsted[scan obscured] Lowery concept defines acids and bases as follows.","تیزابوں اور اساسوں کے آرہینئس نظریے کی حدود پر قابو [scan obscured] ایک زیادہ عمومی تصور سے پایا گیا جسے برونسٹڈ لوری تصور کہتے ہیں۔ برونسٹڈ [scan obscured] لوری تصور تیزابوں اور اساسوں کی تعریف اس طرح کرتا ہے۔","د اسیدونو او القليو د ارهینیوس د تیورۍ محدودیتونه [scan obscured] په یوه ډېره عمومي مفکوره سره لرې شوي چې د برونسټډ-لوري مفکوره بلل کېږي. د برونسټډ [scan obscured] لوري مفکوره اسیدونه او القلي په لاندې ډول تعریفوي.",{"id": "chem11-p243-a1"}),
chem11Pair("An acid is a species (molecule or ion) which donates or tends to donat[scan obscured] proton, whereas, a base is a species (molecule or ion) which accepts or tends[scan obscured] accept a proton.","تیزاب ایک نوع (سالمہ یا آئن) ہے جو پروٹان عطا کرتی ہے یا عطا کرنے کا رجحان رکھتی ہے [scan obscured]، جبکہ اساس ایک نوع (سالمہ یا آئن) ہے جو پروٹان قبول کرتی ہے یا قبول کرنے کا رجحان رکھتی ہے [scan obscured]۔","اسید یو ډول (مالیکول یا آیون) دی چې پروټون ورکوي یا ورکولو تمایل لري [scan obscured]، پداسې حال کې چې القلي یو ډول (مالیکول یا آیون) دی چې پروټون منل کوي یا منلو تمایل لري [scan obscured].",{"id": "chem11-p243-a2"}),
chem11Pair("Tidbit","معلومات","ځانګړې یادونه",{"id": "chem11-p243-t-h", "kind": "heading"}),
chem11Pair("Hydronium ion","ہائیڈرونیم آئن","هایدرونیم آیون",{"id": "chem11-p243-t0", "kind": "heading"}),
chem11Pair("A hydrogen ion (H⁺) is nothing more than a proton and does not exist[scan obscured] itself in an aqueous solution. In water H⁺ combines with water molecule to form[scan obscured] hydrated hydrogen ion (H₃O⁺) commonly called a hydronium ion. For simplicity[scan obscured] it is often used as H⁺ instead of H₃O⁺ in equations, with the clear understanding[scan obscured] that H⁺ is always hydrated in solution.","ہائیڈروجن آئن (H⁺) ایک پروٹان کے سوا کچھ نہیں اور آبی محلول میں تنہا موجود نہیں ہوتا [scan obscured]۔ پانی میں H⁺ پانی کے سالمے کے ساتھ مل کر آبیدہ ہائیڈروجن آئن (H₃O⁺) بناتا ہے جسے عام طور پر ہائیڈرونیم آئن کہتے ہیں [scan obscured]۔ سادگی کی خاطر مساواتوں میں اکثر H₃O⁺ کی جگہ H⁺ استعمال کیا جاتا ہے، اس واضح سمجھ کے ساتھ [scan obscured] کہ محلول میں H⁺ ہمیشہ آبیدہ ہوتا ہے۔","د هایدروجن آیون (H⁺) له پروټون پرته بل څه نه دی او په اوبیز محلول کې پخپله نه شتون لري [scan obscured]. په اوبو کې H⁺ د اوبو له مالیکول سره یوځای کېږي ترڅو هایدریټ شوی هایدروجن آیون (H₃O⁺) جوړ کړي چې معمولاً هایدرونیم آیون بلل کېږي [scan obscured]. د سادګۍ لپاره په معادلو کې ډېری د H₃O⁺ پر ځای H⁺ کارول کېږي، د دې روښانه پوهې سره [scan obscured] چې H⁺ په محلول کې تل هایدریټ وي.",{"id": "chem11-p243-t1"})
]});
